# Implement Audio Generation (Phase 4)

We will implement the final phase of the pipeline by rendering the generated JSON scripts into full audio files using Microsoft's free `edge-tts` library and stitching them together with `pydub`.

## Open Questions

> [!WARNING]
> `pydub` requires **FFmpeg** to be installed on your machine to decode and merge `.mp3` files.
> Do you already have FFmpeg installed and in your system PATH? If not, you will need to download and install it for this to work successfully on Windows.

## Proposed Changes

### `app/services/audio.py`
We will create a dedicated service module for audio generation to keep `tasks.py` clean.
#### [NEW] `app/services/audio.py`
- Create a dictionary mapping characters to voices (e.g., `Dr. Aris -> en-GB-SoniaNeural`, `Captain Vance -> en-US-ChristopherNeural`, `NARRATOR -> en-US-AriaNeural`).
- `generate_line_audio(job_id: int, index: int, speaker: str, text: str) -> str`:
  - Check if `static/audio/chunk_{job_id}_{index}.mp3` exists. If so, skip download.
  - Map the `speaker` to a voice.
  - Execute `edge_tts.Communicate(text, voice).save()` asynchronously.
  - Return the file path.
- `merge_audio(job_id: int, chunk_paths: list[str]) -> str`:
  - Load each chunk sequentially using `pydub.AudioSegment.from_file()`.
  - Concatenate them (`+`).
  - Export the final merged track to `static/audio/final_{job_id}.mp3`.
  - Return the relative URL (e.g., `/static/audio/final_{job_id}.mp3`).

### `app/worker/tasks.py`
Integrate the audio generation into our Celery workflow.
#### [MODIFY] `app/worker/tasks.py`
- After successfully updating the database to `processing_audio`, parse the `script_json`.
- Create a list of asynchronous `generate_line_audio` tasks.
- Use `await asyncio.gather(*tasks)` to run `edge-tts` concurrently for all script lines.
- Call `merge_audio()` to stitch the downloaded chunks.
- Update the job record to `status = "Completed"` and `result_audio_url = final_url`.

### `app/main.py`
Serve the static files so the client can actually listen to the audio.
#### [MODIFY] `app/main.py`
- Add FastAPI's `StaticFiles` mount to serve the `static/audio` directory.

